WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.790
I don't think what happened was your—

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:04.850
Legislator.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.560
Shut up.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.770
Move! You're in the way!

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:08.770
Ow!

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.650
Later, Legislator!

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.340
Wh-What's wrong?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.930
Um... Was it something I did?

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.540
Not you, the Legislator!

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.380
<b>Mystery 6: The Ring</b>

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.760
I knew you were late coming back. 
You went to see the Legislator.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.220
We had plenty of other 
reasons for being late.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.850
What happened?

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.100
You brought back an injured yokai, too.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.150
If you followed my instructions to be careful,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.310
I thought you would be safe...

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.440
<b>Thrilling                 Exciting
Rules for Visiting the 
Underworld: Beginner Edition
1) Don't get lost in the Underworld!
 2) Don't follow strange yokai!
3) Listen to Itsuki and don't quarrel!
4) Say something immediately if you get 
Underworld Sickness and feel unwell!
Dress Code: Clothes Featuring Crest
 Destination: Kiyakudo
Try not to get hurt, and have a safe trip
From the Mononokean</b>

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.650
I'm sorry. I think I probably broke all of them.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.160
Not "probably." You mean "completely."

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.480
You're like a magnet for trouble.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.080
I'm really sorry, everyone.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Do you hate the Underworld now?

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:30.920
Huh?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.540
You seem to have had a scary time.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.010
It was scary, but I brought it all on myself.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.930
A lot of good things happened, too.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.480
I got to meet Koura-san and Shizuku-chan.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.830
The Legislator recognized 
me as an employee, too.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.310
And I got to see Fuzzy again.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.960
You were right.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.820
I'm glad I went to the Underworld.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.700
Thank you, Hanae.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.850
"Thank you"?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.810
I'm sleepy.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.680
So, my daughter is turning five soon...

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.550
<i>Stop bragging about your 
daughter during homeroom.</i>

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.220
<i>We're looking for a ring?</i>

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.560
Did a yokai lose it?

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.790
It's an ordinary wedding ring.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.860
Ordinary?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:46.080
The ring's owner is an old human woman.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.080
An old woman?

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.960
Since her husband passed away,

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.300
she'd been wearing both her own 
and her husband's wedding bands.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.080
But she accidentally dropped her own 
ring while she was out for a walk.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.540
In a creek.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.540
That won't be easy to find.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.500
Our client this time

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.380
is the yokai possessing the husband's ring.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.080
The client's request was to find the lost ring

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.500
and return it to the wife before 
he goes to the Underworld.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.740
That's our job this time.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.100
We've looked for it three times already, 
but we still haven't found it.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.100
I see.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.840
The more people we have,
the easier this job will be.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.100
Will we be meeting the 
client at the usual place?

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.520
Yes, on Monday at 3:30. Don't be late.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.480
<i>It's already past our meeting time!</i>

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.830
<i>I want to go to the convenience store.</i>

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.080
I'll show you guys sometime!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.710
Pictures of my daughter, too!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.000
Hey, teacher.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:40.990
What is it, Fushimi?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.200
Can I go now? I want to go 
to the convenience store.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.300
You talk too much.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.800
<i>Well said, Fusshi!</i>

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.560
Sorry, sorry. It's that time already?

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.360
Okay, homeroom's over.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.810
Be sure you head straight home.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.940
Aw, what?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.160
Fusshi.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.720
Nice play. I'm impressed you 
were able to interrupt him.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.230
I really wanted to go to 
the convenience store,

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.340
but Ashiyan was super pale,

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.100
and Abenon was staring at the 
teacher like he wanted to kill him.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.300
I thought it would end poorly if 
he kept rambling much longer.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.430
You're such a good guy.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:24.380
Huh? I wanted to invite Ashiyan 
to the convenience store.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.550
Oh, he ran out of the classroom 
at the speed of light.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.510
Huh... Maybe he had a stomachache.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.100
Ashiya, what time is it?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.650
3:36.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.660
We're six minutes late.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:46.990
Fuzzy, why don't you stay 
inside the Mononokean?

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.470
You're still hurt.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.300
Don't get excited and move around too 
much just because it's your first job.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.400
There he is.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.710
Sorry we're late, Manjiro.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.390
<i>A snake yokai?</i>

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.640
<i>No, an eel?</i>

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.430
<i>He's got a cute face.</i>

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.330
Abeno! How dare you make your client wait?!

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:25.280
Sorry.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:29.450
Don't think you can slack off just 
because this is our fourth meeting!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.290
Get off me. It hurts.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.380
Who are these two?

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.740
My employees.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:40.440
My name's Ashiya.
Nice to meet you, Manjiro-san.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.080
The guy on my shoulder is Fuzzy.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.710
Don't use them icky honorifics with me.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.530
Call me Manjiro.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.820
Oh... Sure.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.090
<i>An eel straight out of Edo.</i>

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.520
Is this where she lost the ring?

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.900
We've been looking for it for a while.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.670
The current may have washed 
it away. It's pretty fast here.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.480
Wait here, Fuzzy.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.310
You're the only ones who can help me.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.790
So... So no matter how many times it takes,

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:16.290
you're in this with me 
until we find that ring!

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.040
Huh? We know that.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:25.530
What makes you think you 
need to twist our arms now?

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.670
Once we take a job, we never abandon it.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.930
You heard him, Manjiro.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:37.180
We'll definitely find your ring. Don't worry.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.290
Definitely, huh? That's pretty bold.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:48.560
I've always been good at finding metal 
things like earrings and scissors.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.440
Huh? That's a weird talent.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.310
Abeno-san, you'd better give me 
a bonus if I find the ring first.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.910
Hairball, you can search the shore.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.990
You're still hurt, so don't 
push yourself too hard.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:02.590
Now, then...

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.380
I feel like it's over here.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.970
You're going by your instincts?

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.910
And what are you doing with your hands?

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.170
Take this seriously.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.220
I'm being very serious!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.280
You whelps talk a good game.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:19.640
You'd better find it, you little punks.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.730
I told you, we know.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.700
<i>It's not here.</i>

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.240
Manjiro, go back to the old woman.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:48.680
While you're in the mundane 
world, your body can't handle

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:51.030
being away from the husband's ring for long.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.550
Compared to when we first met,

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.390
your body's a lot larger and more unstable.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.390
If you're not careful, you'll disappear.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.350
I know what's happening to me!

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:04.890
Hey!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.400
Just so you know,

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:13.850
if I think you're in danger, even 
if we haven't found your ring,

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.750
I'll forcibly exorcise you.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.020
Abeno-san!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.410
Is this it?

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.760
Abeno-san! Manjiro!

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.250
Is this the ring?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:29.500
<i>Did he really find it using instincts alone?</i>

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.810
It took me fifteen whole minutes to find it.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.760
Hey! Let me see it!

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.170
Here.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.010
No mistake! It's the lady's ring!

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.790
Thanks, kiddo!

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.940
Now we can return the ring to the old lady.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.700
By the way, how are we 
going to return this ring?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.170
How?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.390
We'll just give it to her.

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.540
Like, "Here, we found your ring"?

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.410
Huh? What are you trying to say?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:10.920
If two strange boys suddenly 
showed up to deliver your ring,

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.040
wouldn't you be scared?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.220
Y-You think she'd be scared?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:22.350
It would be scary.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.060
She might even suspect we've broken the law.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:30.570
Abeno-san, did you not have a 
plan for returning the ring?

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.070
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.820
How are we going to return the ring?

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.440
We could put it in her mailbox.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.950
Let's come up with a better way.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.740
What? Why do you care so much 
about how we return the ring?

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:55.280
Well, Manjiro's going to the Underworld 
once we return the ring, right?

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:55.840
Yeah.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.500
Which means this is the last 
time he'll see the old woman.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.500
Manjiro really wanted to 
return the ring to her,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.850
and he came to search the river 
with you a bunch of times.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.130
Instead of just giving it to her,

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:12.350
I was hoping we could tell 
her about Manjiro, too.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.190
<i>Tell her?</i>

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.320
I just think it would be nice 
if we could give her

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.670
something to remember 
Manjiro by before he leaves.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:24.110
Do you have a plan?

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:27.950
H-Hang on. Um, for instance...

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.010
We won't do anything unnecessary.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:36.940
Um, was I being too intrusive?

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:40.600
No, it's not that what you want 
to do is bad or pointless.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:44.720
It's just hard to tell humans 
when yokai are involved.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.720
It just makes them disgusted, suspicious,

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.980
or creeped out.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:51.910
At the very least,

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.070
that's what happens in my experience.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.070
In the worst case scenario,

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.160
she would get suspicious

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.490
and refuse to accept the ring.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.700
The best course of action is

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.490
to finish the job by interacting 
with humans as little as possible.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:15.880
<i>It wasn't that Abeno-san hadn't given any 
thought to how we'd return the ring.</i>

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:19.770
<i>After much thought and experience,</i>

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:22.800
<i>his answer was "don't get involved."</i>

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:25.800
Sorry, Manjiro.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:29.710
I was hoping we could do something,

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.650
but I can't come up with a better way 
to return the ring than Abeno-san's.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.060
I got your hopes up only 
to let you down. I'm sorry.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.520
Raise your head!

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:42.180
Ow!

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.520
I'm sorry...

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.680
That was really loud.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.960
Sorry. I hit you too hard.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.320
Ashiya, I'm not angry.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.380
Huh?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.330
You've done nothing that I'd 
want you to bow to me for.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.850
I appreciate you wanting to tell her,

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.120
but Abeno's right.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.590
If we can't return the ring, then 
all we've done will be for nothing.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.030
Let's return it quietly without 
the old lady noticing.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:13.100
I'll be satisfied as long as 
we're able to return the ring.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.620
Manjiro...

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.320
Fuzzy?

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.700
Hairball?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:29.160
It seems the fuzzball's 
accepting your idea, Abeno.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.780
We're all agreed, then.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:40.010
Manjiro, take us to her house.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.090
Sure. It's not far.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.800
Put the ring in her mailbox,
and she'll be sure to find it.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.590
<i>Not telling her is the best way.</i>

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.310
<i>It makes sense in my head, but...</i>

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.350
Let's go.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:56.760
Okay.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:02.220
<i>But I can't stop wondering</i>

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.090
<i>if there's another way.</i>

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:17.160
This is her house.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.270
I should've summoned the Mononokean.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.640
Manjiro, you've been going all 
the way to the river from here?

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:25.690
At this distance, I would've taken a bike.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.170
You kids lack stamina.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:31.720
It looks like it's closed now, 
but what kind of shop was this?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.340
An eel shop.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:34.930
Ah.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.040
Is this the mailbox?

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.440
She doesn't use this one.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.200
Come around back.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.280
Is she out?

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.450
No, the lights are on, 
so she's probably inside.

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:54.280
This is the mailbox.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:08.840
<i>Now we put the ring in the 
mailbox, and it's over.</i>

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.480
<i>There's so much I want to tell her.</i>

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.750
<i>Humans can't see yokai,</i>

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.140
<i>so the yokai are stuck on an 
emotional one-way street.</i>

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.650
<i>I wonder why humans can't see them.</i>

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:24.650
<i>If humans could see yokai, too,</i>

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.860
<i>they would understand everything.</i>

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:28.570
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.550
<i>"If humans could see them, too..."</i>

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.270
<i>Then what about me?</i>

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:39.420
Ashiya?

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.120
Who are you?

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:42.830
Oops!

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:45.090
You idiot! What are you doing?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.170
Hey! What are you doing in front of my house?

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:50.550
Abeno-san?

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.560
<i>This sucks.</i>

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.680
You, too. What were you 
trying to put in my mailbox?

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:58.540
This is, um...

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.850
My ring?

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.980
Why do you have this?

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.440
Um...

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.240
Don't say anything.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:13.550
But—

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.610
No buts!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:23.370
Ashiya, shake her hand off and 
put the ring in the mailbox.

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:25.290
She's an old woman.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.190
It should be easy enough to pull away.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.210
Do it.

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.470
I told you not to get involved with humans.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:35.470
Abeno-san...

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.620
We're human, too.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.400
We can see everything and hear everything.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:45.820
We know everything.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.900
Whether or not they'd understand aside,

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.500
if we ignore humans,

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.490
then they truly never will understand.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:59.530
So I won't shake her off.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.870
Um, why don't we at least tell her his name?

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:12.840
<i>I completely pissed him off!</i>

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.220
<i>I'm an idiot!</i>

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.080
<i>You understood Abeno-san's logic, you idiot!</i>

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:22.600
"Humans" this, "seeing" that...

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.810
Did you come to discuss philosophy with me?

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:26.170
Huh? Philosophy?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:30.650
I'm sorry. I'm panicking right now 
and have no idea what you're saying.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.980
Hey, Ashiya.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:35.520
I appreciate the thought,

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.580
but we need to get out of here.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.030
Put the ring in her mailbox.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:40.740
Manjiro.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:41.720
What?

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.840
Someone named Manjiro

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.510
asked us to give that ring to you.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:49.930
Manjiro?

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:55.170
Yes. He said the ring was 
very important to you.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:59.820
Given that I can't explain any more 
than this about what we're doing,

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.260
I understand you have 
no reason to believe us,

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:07.560
but I hope you'll keep the ring regardless.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:13.860
What?

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:18.860
<i>Yeah, I knew it.</i>

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:22.260
<i>I knew this would happen, but I...</i>

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.030
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.870
<i>This is why I was told to do nothing.</i>

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.860
<i>If she refuses to take the ring now...</i>

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:33.290
Um—

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.120
Ashiya!

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.880
Don't say anything.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.620
<i>It's all... It's all my fault.</i>

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.890
<i>I shouldn't have thought about it.</i>

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:50.770
<i>I shouldn't have done anything.</i>

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:51.880
<i>I shouldn't have...</i>

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.150
I see.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.540
I see.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.340
Manjiro asked you to do it.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:08.410
Ma'am?

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:13.170
Looks like you were bewitched 
by Manjiro's ghost.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.800
What? You know Manjiro?

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.670
I'm very familiar with that name.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:22.550
Manjiro was my husband's name.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.070
What?!

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:26.310
He passed away long ago, though.

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:32.010
Maybe he appeared because I lost the ring.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:34.810
I can't believe he got you two involved.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.320
Still, I thought I'd never find it.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.320
I'm so happy.

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:43.740
You.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.320
Yes?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:48.200
I'll take the ring.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.570
Thanks for delivering it.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.190
<i>Did she understand?</i>

00:19:56.370 --> 00:20:00.090
No, thank you.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.670
Raise your head.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:05.130
Ma'am, hold out your hand.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.480
We returned the ring, Manjiro.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.490
Manjiro.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:27.330
Thank you, Manjiro.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:29.820
Sure!

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:45.750
<i>When did I stop telling people about yokai?</i>

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.790
<i>If we ignore humans,</i>

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:51.440
<i>then they truly never will understand.</i>

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.920
<i>I think I'd given up on hoping</i>

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:56.520
<i>they'd understand long before then.</i>

00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:01.430
<i>Once I gave up, I closed 
my eyes to everything.</i>

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.700
<i>But...</i>

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:08.200
<i>Even if they can't see them, 
I guess they can still understand.</i>

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:13.750
Oh, I know. You can have dinner at my place.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:14.640
What?

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.750
I need to thank you for finding the ring.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.140
You don't need to thank us.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.310
Don't be shy.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.630
Stay for dinner.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.120
Okay, then I accept your offer.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:26.650
Why do we have to stay 
for dinner? Hey, Ashi—

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.890
Found you.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.380
How about some eel?

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.020
Huh?!

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:37.820
Ashiya.

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:38.650
Yes?

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:42.030
Did you see anything just now?

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.530
No. Is something wrong?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.030
No.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:50.900
It's nothing.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time "The Encounter"</b>

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:29.050
I thought I sensed a strange 
presence. Was it my imagination?

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:33.880
Now that you mention it, I hear a 
suspicious tap, tap, tapping sound.

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.370
Abeno-san, could this be...

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:38.580
That's the sound of Manjiro's 
wife cutting a daikon.
